    "title": "'Aggressive' Attempt to Dismiss James Comey Case Unlikely to Succeed: Veteran Trial Lawyer",
    "text": "Senior counsel at the Lawfare Project Gerard Filitti says the most striking part of former FBI director James Comey’s arraignment in Virginia on Wednesday is the defense’s plan to have the case dismissed on vindictive or selective prosecution grounds. Filitti says this shows Comey’s attorneys will seek to make the case very public and will be arguing about the politics behind it, not just the law.\n‘Aggressive’ Attempt to Dismiss James Comey Case Unlikely to Succeed: Veteran Trial Lawyer\nGerard Filitti, senior counsel, discussed Comey’s attorneys potentially seeking to make the case very public and arguing about the politics, not just the law.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/8/2025, 11:59:29 PM EDT",
